course: dictionary
lesson: 13469
title: Hydrated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hydrated means having enough water in your body. When you are hydrated, you are not thirsty or dried out. «Sam drank three glasses of water after football, so he stayed hydrated.» Stayed hydrated means he had enough water in his body.
explain: Hydrated is also the past form of the verb hydrate, which means to give water or moisture. «The gardener hydrated the dry plants with a watering can.» Here hydrated means the plants were given water.
explain: In science, a hydrated crystal has water joined to it inside its structure. «The blue crystals were hydrated copper sulphate.» Look at the words around hydrated to decide which meaning fits, then check by putting your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Hydrated means having enough water in your body.
fact: «Hydrated» is the past form of the verb «hydrate»: «The plants were hydrated.»
fact: «Stay hydrated» means drink enough water, especially in hot weather and during sport.
fact: In science, hydrated crystals contain water; heating them drives the water off, and blue copper sulphate turns white.
fact: On a skincare bottle, «hydrated» means moist.
exercise: «Sam drank three glasses of water after football, so he stayed hydrated.» What does hydrated mean here? | Very tired after running | Wet from the rain | *Having enough water in your body | Thirsty and dried out
exercise: «The gardener hydrated the dry plants with a watering can.» What does hydrated mean here? | Painted green | *Given water | Cut down | Covered in soil
exercise: Which phrase means drink enough water, especially in hot weather? | *Stay hydrated | Stay up late | Keep the lights on | Stay in bed
test: On a skincare bottle, «hydrated» means what? | Dusty and rough | Very cold | *Moist | Dry and cracked
test: Which is true about hydrated copper sulphate? | It has no water inside it | It is made of sugar | *It has water joined to it in its crystals | It is always green
exam: Mia says, «I am hydrated, so I don't need to drink today.» Why might her idea be wrong? | Hydrated means hungry, so she should eat instead | Hydrated means tired, so she should sleep more | *Being hydrated means having enough water now, but the body uses water all day, so she should keep drinking
